WEBVTT

00:00:10.030 --> 00:00:12.490
<i>I have no interest in world peace.</i>

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:17.990
<i>And in doing so, my world is peaceful.</i>

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.700
This was the way that Marco Polo
was introduced to Japan.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.330
<i>People lie...</i>

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.080
Be sure to remember this, guys.
It's important.

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:25.250
<i>At school, at work...</i>

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:29.800
<i>To an unbelievable degree,
people live to lie.</i>

00:00:35.470 --> 00:00:36.890
It's so cold today.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:45.690
That will be 520 yen, please.

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:52.190
Thanks so much.

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:59.780
You'd look so much cuter
if you put your bangs back.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:07.920
I-I'm sorry!

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.340
Just stop it, okay?

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.340
Apparently she has a little crush.

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:16.090
Stop.

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:17.180
That's right.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.010
Stop teasing her!

00:01:29.150 --> 00:01:30.690
<i>I just can't do it.</i>

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:34.030
<i>Speaking so naturally about things...</i>

00:01:35.070 --> 00:01:36.360
<i>exaggerating themselves...</i>

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.570
<i>with no sense of unease at all...</i>

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:43.080
<i>flirting and laughing with each other.</i>

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:49.830
<i>At that time, I still hadn't known.</i>

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:55.380
<i>I hadn't known that after December 24, 2016,</i>

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:59.720
<i>my world would be chilled in bright light,
dazzled by darkness,</i>

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:04.350
<i>and heated by warmth
that I thought would drive me mad.</i>

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:09.270
<i>I didn't know it would scorch me.</i>

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:50.750
Goodbye Small World

00:03:56.130 --> 00:04:00.050
P-Production GIP?

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:05.590
"Hello. Please forgive this sudden letter.

00:04:05.590 --> 00:04:09.220
I am from Production GIP.

00:04:09.220 --> 00:04:14.600
We have chosen you, Takigawa Miu,
to be a member in our new project."

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:17.310
What is this?

00:04:19.150 --> 00:04:21.900
Big Sister! Welcome back!

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.280
Hey, Haru. I'm home.

00:04:25.160 --> 00:04:26.450
Where's Mom?

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:27.240
In bed!

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:30.870
Welcome back, Miu. You sure worked hard.

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:32.410
How're you feeling?

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.420
Hmm. About the same as usual.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:38.090
Okay. I'll go get dinner started.

00:04:38.460 --> 00:04:39.670
Thanks.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:43.050
Yay! Dinner! Dinner!

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:06.530
Going into show biz...

00:05:07.620 --> 00:05:09.830
This letter is mocking me.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:17.920
Where would I find the time
to do any of that?

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:31.350
I came anyway.
What the heck am I doing here?

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:37.730
Hey, are you possibly...

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:40.020
I thought so!

00:05:40.020 --> 00:05:43.030
I was thinking that it
wasn't just me that got picked!

00:05:40.560 --> 00:05:46.200
Sakura Fujima

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:46.200
My name's Fujima Sakura.
Nice to meet you!

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:50.070
I-I'm Takigawa Miu.

00:05:50.070 --> 00:05:53.040
Miu! Your name is so cute!

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:56.830
It's my first time coming to this zoo,
and I'm totally lost.

00:05:56.830 --> 00:05:58.790
Why are we meeting
in front of the gorillas?

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:00.250
It's a total mystery!

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:02.090
Ah, yeah, um...

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:05.300
And speaking of mysteries,
let's talk about GIP!

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:10.390
Rumor is they've been going around, sending letters
to all the cute girls in Japan for this new project!

00:06:10.390 --> 00:06:11.350
To have them audition?

00:06:11.720 --> 00:06:16.060
Yeah! So all the girls around here today
must be here for GIP!

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:20.940
I knew I shouldn't have come.

00:06:20.940 --> 00:06:22.610
And that includes you, Miu!

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:25.570
Your skin is so smooth and pale,

00:06:25.570 --> 00:06:27.570
and your legs are so svelte and skinny.

00:06:27.950 --> 00:06:28.990
No...

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:33.870
I'm glad that there's someone
I can get along with here.

00:06:39.750 --> 00:06:42.750
Toda Jun

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.750
Th-The gorilla's looking at me!

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:49.840
I'm so scared!
I'm gonna turn into gorilla food!

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:52.890
I don't want to get eaten!

00:06:53.220 --> 00:06:55.510
I don't think gorillas eat humans.

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:57.310
No, that's a lie!

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:59.850
That one was looking at me like,
"She must be delicious!"

00:07:00.230 --> 00:07:02.810
He's probably deciding
to use ketchup or sauce on me!

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:06.820
Hey, you.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:10.150
I'm waiting for someone to meet me
for some very important business.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:13.620
Reika Sato

00:07:10.700 --> 00:07:13.620
If you're going to cause such a scene,
would you mind doing it elsewhere?

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.330
Ah! It's a lady gorilla!

00:07:15.530 --> 00:07:17.330
Huh?! Where?

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:21.000
Wait. I don't see any of those anywhere!

00:07:22.500 --> 00:07:25.210
Um, does your very important business
have to do with this?

00:07:27.250 --> 00:07:28.300
You got one, too?

00:07:28.300 --> 00:07:29.590
I did, too!

00:07:30.260 --> 00:07:31.970
Y-You, too?

00:07:33.390 --> 00:07:36.060
I'm Toda Jun. Nice to meet you!

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:39.480
Hey! Where are you going?

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:42.480
I regret coming here in the first place!

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:45.730
If they chose children like you,
they must be pulling a fast one on me!

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:48.480
Hey, that's awfully mean of you!

00:07:48.480 --> 00:07:51.450
Pardon me.
Are all of you also waiting to audition?

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:52.400
Audition?

00:07:53.110 --> 00:07:57.120
I couldn't help overhearing, and you're
all quite pretty, so I thought...

00:07:53.610 --> 00:07:57.120
Maruyama Akane

00:07:58.490 --> 00:08:02.290
What's with the surprise attack?
Praising me is going to be useless!

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:05.290
I did not intend to attack you.

00:08:05.290 --> 00:08:06.670
I was merely speaking the truth.

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:08.090
T-Truth?!

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:09.630
Hey, excuse me.

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:14.260
Tachikawa Ayaka

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:13.930
Seems like this is the meeting place.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:16.220
Yeah, that's right!

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:18.970
How did you know
we were project candidates?

00:08:18.970 --> 00:08:20.680
Because you're all really cute?

00:08:20.680 --> 00:08:22.310
You probably were listening to us!

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:25.480
Oh, your legs are so nice!
Aren't you cold?

00:08:25.810 --> 00:08:28.820
I'm fine. After all, this is an audition, right?

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:32.950
I'm gonna have to use
every trick in the book to charm the judges.

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:35.990
Charm them? How vulgar!

00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:37.700
Sexy!

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.160
See? Thanks!

00:08:40.160 --> 00:08:42.080
Where'd you buy those clothes?

00:08:42.080 --> 00:08:46.130
- Omotesando, I think.
- That's a weird name for a store!

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:45.080
It's nice having everyone here
and talking like this.

00:08:45.080 --> 00:08:46.670
Y-You think?

00:08:46.670 --> 00:08:48.750
Hey, all of you over there,
you're being loud.

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:53.720
I'm trying to read.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:58.850
Seems like the quality of Japan's
entertainment industry has plummeted.

00:08:58.850 --> 00:08:59.680
Huh?

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:01.770
Oh, so you, too?

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:03.480
Well, I wonder.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:06.060
If all of you other candidates
are this unpleasant,

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:08.150
Nicole Saito

00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:08.150
I might just head home in five minutes.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.700
Ah, I made it!

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:18.240
Man, Tokyo's subways
are a real devil to navigate!

00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:20.280
It was like some maze experiment.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:24.410
I'm not a guinea pig!
They multiply at the drop of a hat!

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:30.500
Looks like I'm in the right place!
You all appear to have letters, too.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:34.130
And we're all on time.
That's productive members of society for you.

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:37.010
Still, Ueno Station is a busy place!
Look at all these people!

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:37.010
<i>She's not entirely all there, is she?</i>

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.050
I'm Miyako!

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:43.770
Kono Miyako

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:41.180
Where there's nothing, there's me-yako!

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:43.770
I'm Osaka's favorite
big-mouthed girl, Miyako Kono!

00:09:44.060 --> 00:09:47.600
I thought of that on the train. How was it?

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:49.560
Give me a reaction!

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:52.020
I mean, even if you ask me
to tell you how it was...

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:53.780
Baby!

00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:56.490
That was great! Let me do one, too!

00:09:57.030 --> 00:09:59.450
It's the same as a kabuki prologue,
but it's for idols!

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:59.450
That makes eight of us now.

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:02.580
You see, you gotta be unique!

00:10:06.160 --> 00:10:08.330
G-Gorilla!

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.080
A-A gorilla?!

00:10:10.080 --> 00:10:11.750
He must've escaped his cage!

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:13.340
Save me, Mom!

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:16.670
Thank you all for gathering.

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:19.180
MANAGER
AOI GOUDA

00:10:18.050 --> 00:10:21.050
My name is Goda, and I'm with GIP.

00:10:24.270 --> 00:10:26.480
GIP, like from the letter?

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:31.610
I would like the eight of you to make
your major-label debut as an idol group with us.

00:10:33.020 --> 00:10:34.690
Major-label debut?

00:10:34.690 --> 00:10:36.860
You mean we don't need to audition?

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:38.990
There will be no auditions.

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:40.070
What?

00:10:40.070 --> 00:10:42.320
The selection process has already ended.

00:10:42.740 --> 00:10:46.790
You eight did not come here by chance.
You have been chosen.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:48.660
We were chosen...

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:50.420
B-But why?

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:53.000
I played a tree in a play
for our school culture festival,

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:54.880
and I barely passed music.

00:10:54.880 --> 00:10:56.420
And I'm telling you that's fine.

00:10:57.800 --> 00:11:00.720
We're looking for new idols.

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:06.060
If you could please come with me,
it would be faster to just show you.

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:15.440
Hold on! Are you really going to believe
such a fishy story?

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:10.830
What...

00:12:12.040 --> 00:12:14.290
Wh-What the heck is this place?!

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:16.540
Wow, it's so big!

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:21.050
This place... we're under—

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:22.470
Underneath the zoo.

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:24.640
Please take one.

00:12:24.640 --> 00:12:26.100
Many, many thanks!

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:54.210
So what do you think?

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:57.040
This entire facility was built
for what we're starting here today.

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:02.090
You could say it's an embodiment
of our hopes for you.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:06.390
Do you think it is an agreeable place
for you to work in?

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:11.890
As the last part of our tour,
let me show you to our most important room.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:18.730
This is your room.

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:20.980
Whoa!

00:13:28.820 --> 00:13:32.370
While in the office,
you'll be on standby here in this room.

00:13:41.250 --> 00:13:43.050
What is this?

00:13:43.420 --> 00:13:44.420
The Wall.

00:13:45.760 --> 00:13:47.300
The Wall?

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:50.390
We don't know some of the finer details
about it quite yet.

00:13:50.970 --> 00:13:55.060
We just know that it spits out orders
at indeterminate intervals.

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:59.270
It spits them out?
How can it when it's not alive?

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:03.280
When it issues orders, we must obey and deliver
what it asks of us without exception.

00:14:03.530 --> 00:14:05.780
Obey? What does that mean?

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:07.740
Orders?

00:14:07.740 --> 00:14:14.160
I cannot say. All I do know is that
it hasn't issued any orders as of yet.

00:14:14.160 --> 00:14:18.000
So we don't even know why we were chosen?

00:14:18.000 --> 00:14:21.000
We have to blindly obey something
when we don't know its goals?

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:22.800
Correct.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:25.630
Wow, what an idol!

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:29.550
Unfortunately, the Wall
is this project's absolute source.

00:14:35.560 --> 00:14:37.850
I don't get any of this.

00:14:37.850 --> 00:14:40.730
This Wall is super weird!
And scary, too!

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:43.070
Wall, Orders, Obey, Absolute, Idol

00:14:42.520 --> 00:14:44.900
There are too many unknown factors here.

00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:48.030
B-But the facility we saw upstairs
was well-built, right?

00:14:48.400 --> 00:14:51.160
Yeah, they definitely pumped
lots of money into building it.

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:54.240
I don't think they used all that money
for a big grift, you know?

00:14:54.740 --> 00:14:58.580
It doesn't seem like some rich person
made this to occupy themselves.

00:14:58.580 --> 00:15:00.420
What do you mean by "rich person"?

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:02.590
You tell me, modern girl.

00:15:02.590 --> 00:15:03.960
What did you say?!

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:05.340
Are you all stupid?

00:15:06.460 --> 00:15:10.050
It doesn't matter who we're working for.
This is a chance we've been given.

00:15:10.050 --> 00:15:10.930
A chance?

00:15:11.930 --> 00:15:15.890
If we've been given the path to become stars,
then we should certainly use it.

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:18.020
A chance, huh?

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:19.690
Miu, what do you—

00:15:20.640 --> 00:15:21.480
Huh?

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:23.860
Miu?

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:33.240
<i>It's as if I'm in another world,
and not in my own.</i>

00:15:33.990 --> 00:15:35.200
Where are you going?

00:15:36.540 --> 00:15:37.580
I'm going home.

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:39.750
I didn't sign up for this.

00:15:40.710 --> 00:15:43.670
You have until December 24th,
a week from now.

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:46.550
The eight of you will officially begin
your formation on that date.

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:49.720
This is a foregone conclusion.

00:15:49.720 --> 00:15:51.260
You will return.

00:15:58.060 --> 00:16:00.640
<i>This is not something
that has started recently.</i>

00:16:00.640 --> 00:16:03.190
<i>Adults are creatures
who have always said selfish things.</i>

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:07.150
<i>Did they think by telling us we were chosen
that we would be happy?</i>

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:11.700
<i>It just means someone else
wasn't chosen when I was.</i>

00:16:14.490 --> 00:16:17.660
<i>There are those who live their lives
without being chosen.</i>

00:16:17.660 --> 00:16:20.660
<i>There are also those
who care nothing for other's feelings.</i>

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:24.880
<i>Irresponsibly, mercilessly,
they segregate things.</i>

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:29.510
<i>The world is made up of adults like those.</i>

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:33.380
<i>Idols are fools.</i>

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:36.890
Heave-ho. Heave-ho.

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:39.350
Big Sister!

00:16:40.430 --> 00:16:42.180
<i>This is where I should be.</i>

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:46.980
<i>These two are...</i>

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:49.400
<i>my entire world.</i>

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:59.160
What the heck? That's hilarious!

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:02.660
Takigawa, a word, please.

00:17:07.590 --> 00:17:10.130
What do you mean
I don't need to come in anymore?

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:14.510
No, please don't! I need this job!

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:18.720
The other girls say they're afraid of you
and you make their job harder.

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:23.930
That puts us in a bind, you see.
We prize teamwork here above all else.

00:17:25.350 --> 00:17:28.060
You may not be cut out for customer service.

00:17:28.060 --> 00:17:31.820
Customers have complained in the past
that you're not friendly enough.

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:34.990
They also say that they've never
seen you smile.

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:39.280
I-I'm not very good at smiling
in front of people.

00:17:39.780 --> 00:17:41.580
Not good at it, huh?

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:52.250
Listen, work is like shoveling snow.

00:17:54.010 --> 00:17:56.550
Of course you'd shovel snow
for your own house, right?

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:59.850
And if you shovel snow for others,
you can receive money.

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:04.520
You do things you don't want to,
that's why they call it work.

00:18:14.440 --> 00:18:15.240
Big Sister...

00:18:15.570 --> 00:18:17.860
have you been writing songs lately?

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:20.950
I haven't heard you playing your piano.

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:25.750
I want to hear it again sometime!

00:18:25.750 --> 00:18:29.670
Going to one of Big Sister's concerts
is a dream of mine!

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:30.920
Don't say that.

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:35.970
Big Sister?

00:18:40.260 --> 00:18:42.560
Please don't ever say that again!

00:18:44.640 --> 00:18:45.520
Miu?

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:47.560
Did something happen?

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:52.980
If something's happened, you need to tell me.

00:18:56.070 --> 00:18:57.700
No, nothing.

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:00.610
Just rest, okay, Mom?

00:19:03.030 --> 00:19:03.870
Miu...

00:19:20.550 --> 00:19:21.930
I can give you 1,400 yen for it.

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:25.890
Can't you give me a bit more?

00:19:26.470 --> 00:19:29.890
It's a pretty old model.
You'll get similar offers elsewhere.

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:48.870
<i>People lie...</i>

00:19:50.160 --> 00:19:53.670
<i>to friends, lovers,
even their parents sometimes.</i>

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:58.670
<i>They say lies they don't want to say
as often as possible.</i>

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:17.570
THANK YOU

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:31.960
It's time. Please begin.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:34.210
B-But Miu isn't...

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:36.790
She ran off last time, didn't she?

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:39.460
I don't want to team up
with people who don't want to do this.

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:44.010
H-Hey, you don't have to go that far,
and she might've had a reason to—

00:20:44.010 --> 00:20:45.680
The crossroads of life.

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:48.890
That's why everyone came here, right?

00:20:50.100 --> 00:20:53.440
If she did have a reason,
then that's her answer.

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:57.360
Um, do you think you might be able
to wait a bit longer for her?

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:01.740
I think she's going to come.

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:04.700
Miu will surely come.

00:21:05.660 --> 00:21:07.200
And on what basis—

00:21:14.250 --> 00:21:15.880
We've been waiting for you.

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:19.000
I didn't come here for you!

00:21:21.340 --> 00:21:22.970
I hate adults.

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:26.890
They segregate, command,
direct and force.

00:21:26.890 --> 00:21:28.930
They do those selfish things,
and I hate it!

00:21:29.310 --> 00:21:30.890
Idols are no better.

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:35.810
They laugh at stupid things, wear frilly outfits,
and shake their butts for their customers.

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:37.020
It's foolish!

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:40.650
If that is the case, then why are you here?

00:21:41.190 --> 00:21:44.360
I have come here
to do the job I want to do the least.

00:21:45.200 --> 00:21:48.320
And if I want to become an adult,
I need to become good at it.

00:21:48.990 --> 00:21:51.870
If I must do it to protect
the ones most precious to me...

00:21:52.790 --> 00:21:54.960
I'll become the world's top idol.

00:21:54.960 --> 00:21:56.580
I'll do anything!

00:22:06.590 --> 00:22:08.720
<i>We still didn't know.</i>

00:22:09.300 --> 00:22:12.680
<i>We didn't know the real reason
why the eight of us were assembled...</i>

00:22:13.390 --> 00:22:16.140
<i>nor the grand fate awaiting us
within that maelstrom.</i>

00:22:18.810 --> 00:22:24.190
<i>Nor did we know the meaning
of the being that was named 22/7.</i>

00:22:19.360 --> 00:22:25.990
WELCOME TO 22/7

00:23:54.990 --> 00:24:00.000
Episode 2: In the Middle of Being Dizzy

00:23:57.620 --> 00:23:59.250
"In the Middle of Being Dizzy."
